Package: dns-panel
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Sergey Denisov <4402989@gmail.com>
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/ds1919/dns-panel
Depends: perl, libcgi-pm-perl, libdbi-perl, libdbd-mysql-perl, libjson-perl, libwww-perl, libcrypt-urandom-perl,
 libcrypt-argon2-perl, libcryptx-perl, libauth-googleauth-perl, libimager-qrcode-perl, apache2, libapache2-mod-fcgid,
 libfcgi-perl, bind9-dnsutils, curl, iproute2, mariadb-server, mariadb-client,
 pdns-server (>= 5.1), pdns-server (<< 5.2), pdns-backend-mysql (>= 5.1)
Conflicts: pdns-backend-bind
Description: web panel for PowerDNS as the hidden primary of an internal DNS
 Zones and records, distribution to secondaries (catalog zones, AXFR, TSIG), DNSSEC, migration from BIND,
 dynamic DNS, an active/standby pair, NS Pulse, users and permissions with an audit log, HTTP API and MCP.
 Installs a standalone node into /opt/dns-panel; a pair is built later in the panel.
 PowerDNS 5.1 comes from repo.powerdns.com: add it first with powerdns-repo.sh from the release.
